Log one structured "evaluation finished" record per evaluation.

Nothing recorded how close an evaluation came to its memory ceiling,
whether the kernel killed part of it, or which evaluator ran. The
runner now logs one JSON line through nixbot's logger after the
evaluator exits and before the evaluation's cgroup is removed: the
build id, the evaluator and its version (NIXBOT_EVALUATOR, "<name>
<version>"), workers and per-worker memory limit, wall time, the
cgroup's memory.max, memory.peak, memory.events oom_kill and cpu.stat
user/system time, the number of nix-eval-jobs stderr lines reporting a
worker killed for the memory budget or killed by something else, and
the exit status. It is written on success, failure and timeout, and it
carries no text from the evaluator's output. A cgroup file the kernel
does not provide, or an evaluation without its own cgroup, leaves the
corresponding fields out.

